WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.925
First: who creates a G M S A in
production under the standard?

3
00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:11.031
The answer is b: the pipeline,
as G M S A dash M S A pipe,

4
00:00:11.031 --> 00:00:16.575
running Chapter 6's approved plan
with only the delegated rights.

5
00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:19.005
SailPoint never writes a G M S A,

6
00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:23.088
and ServiceNow's Active
Directory spoke isn't used.

7
00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:27.912
Second: an R two G M S A was
last certified seven months ago.

8
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:29.701
What does Chapter 12 report?

9
00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:34.217
The answer is b: N P I S T D
twenty, certification overdue,

10
00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:37.913
because R two is certified
every six months.

11
00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:40.340
The module page has three more questions,

12
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.890
each linked to the
section that answers it.
